{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@preconcurrency"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"map"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transformed"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"transform"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@escaping"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncSequence\/Element"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transformed"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncThrowingMapSequence","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncThrowingMapSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transformed"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"transform","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mapping closure. "},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" accepts an element"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of this sequence as its parameter and returns a transformed value of the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"same or of a different type. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"type":"text","text":" can also throw an error, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ends the transformed sequence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An asynchronous sequence that contains, in order, the elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produced by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"text":" closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method to transform every element received from a base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous sequence. Typically, you use this to transform from one type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of element to another."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this example, an asynchronous sequence called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5"},{"type":"text","text":". The closure provided to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" and looks up a corresponding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"romanNumeralDict"},{"type":"text","text":" dictionary. This means the outer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterates over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" instances instead of the underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces. Also, the dictionary doesn’t provide a key for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4"},{"type":"text","text":", and the closure throws an error for any key it can’t look up, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receiving this value from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" ends the modified sequence with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let romanNumeralDict: [Int: String] =","    [1: \"I\", 2: \"II\", 3: \"III\", 5: \"V\"]","","do {","    let stream = Counter(howHigh: 5)","        .map { (value) throws -> String in","            guard let roman = romanNumeralDict[value] else {","                throw MyError()","            }","            return roman","        }","    for try await numeral in stream {","        print(numeral, terminator: \" \")","    }","} catch {","    print(\"Error: \\(error)\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"I II III Error: MyError() \""],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"map(_:)","externalID":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF::SYNTHESIZED::s:12_Concurrency19AsyncFilterSequenceV","symbolKind":"method","platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","dep